  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Use model factory for pooling:\n      - Refactor pooling to rely on model factory/registration instead of type constructors. Lucifer now runs class constructors for LuciferModel and LuciferPool at startup and LuciferPool static ctor registers all PooledObject types via Lucifer.SetModelT.\n      - Removed many generic new() constraints from PooledObject APIs (Dispatch, Rent, Return, Pool<T>, HttpModel<T>, etc.) and changed Pool<T>to create instances with Lucifer.GetModelT<T>().\n      - LogManager now rents Utf8Builder instances and pre-reserves 256KB caches instead of allocating directly. Simplified byte-array pool helpers and removed debug tracking; several buffer/Utf8Builder constructors were removed to enforce usage of pooled instances.",
